  "result": "I fixed the bug. `IntRange(0, min_open=True, clamp=True).convert('0', None, None)` now returns 1 instead of -1. `python -m pytest tests/test_types.py -q` gives 43 passed and 2 skipped.\n\n- **Fix:** In `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py`, I changed `bound - dir` to `bound + dir`. The caller passes `dir=1` for the min bound and `dir=-1` for the max bound, meaning the direction to move into the range. The old subtraction moved the value out of the range for both bounds.\n- **Tests:** I added two cases to the clamp parametrize list at the top of `tests/test_types.py`. One is `IntRange(0, min_open=True, clamp=True)` with `\"0\"`, expecting 1. The other is `IntRange(max=5, max_open=True, clamp=True)` with `\"5\"`, expecting 4.\n\nI did not run the full suite, only `tests/test_types.py`.",
